---
title: Spice-Coated Rack of Lamb with Arugula, Avocado, and Blood Orange Salad
servings: 2
source: http://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/Spice-Coated-Rack-of-Lamb-for-Two-with-Arugula-Avocado-and-Blood-Orange-Salad-351234
tags: Lamb
---

= Lamb =
Pre-heat oven to 400°F.
In a small bowl, mix @cumin{2%tsp}, @unsweetened cocoa powder{1%tbsp}, @ground coffee{1%tbsp}(mild roast), and @black pepper{1/2%tsp}.

Rub exposed @rack of lamb{24%oz} bones with @canola oil{1%tbsp}, then wrap each bone in foil, covering bones completely and leaving meat uncovered.
Sprinkle both sides of uncovered lamb with @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp}, then rub with spice mixture.

In a heavy #12" oven-safe sauté pan{} over high heat, heat @canola oil{1%tbsp} until hot but not smoking.
Sear rack, meat side down, moving occasionally to prevent sticking, until deep golden brown and crust forms, about 2 minutes.
Flip to sear underside in same manner, about 2 minutes, then sear bottom of rack in same manner, 2 minutes more.

Flip rack back to meat side up, then transfer pan to oven and roast ~{7%minutes}.
Add @unsalted butter{2%tbsp}, @garlic{2%cloves}(peeled and smashed), and @fresh thyme{3%sprigs} to pan
and continue roasting until thermometer inserted 2 inches into thickest part of lamb (do not touch bone)
registers 130°F (for medium rare), 7 to 8 minutes more.

Tilt pan to collect juices and spoon those over meat.
Transfer lamb to rack with pan or plate underneath to catch juices and let rest ~{10%minutes}.

= Salad =
In small bowl, whisk together @blood orange juice{1/4%cup}, @shallot{1%tbsp}(minced),
@sea salt{1/2%tsp}, and @black pepper{1/4%tsp}.
Gradually add @extra-virgin olive oil{2%tbsp} and whisk vigorously to combine.
(Vinaigrette can be prepared ahead and refrigerated, covered, up to 2 days. Whisk thoroughly before using.)

= Serving =
Peel and cut an @avocado{1} into 1/4" slices.
Divide the avocado between two plates, fanning out slices over half of plate.
Top with @baby arugula{2%cups} and drizzle with vinaigrette.
Top with @blood orange{1}(peeled, segmented, and seeded) segments and sprinkle with @sea salt{1/4%tsp}, and @black pepper{1/4%tsp}.

Remove foil from lamb bones.
Slice rack into 4 double chops and transfer to plates alongside salad.
Serve immediately.
